	<p>
		The main project is <strong>OpenClaw</strong>: a local-first autonomous AI platform that runs
		natively on a <strong>Mac Mini and Mac Studio</strong> in my home office. It runs five
		specialised agents &mdash; coding, orchestration, reasoning, workflows, and auditing &mdash;
		alongside its own gateway, cron jobs, memory store, and channels into Telegram and Discord.
		Qwen3.6 handles the routine work locally, with Codex (via free ChatGPT OAuth) and Claude Opus
		on tap for the heavy lifting. Total cloud cost: $0.
	</p>

	<p>
		Day to day I drive <strong>Claude Code</strong> and the <strong>Codex CLI</strong> for almost
